#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Improving Expectation Values: Propagated Noise Absorption (PNA)"
msgstr "Meningkatkan Nilai Ekspektasi: Propagated Noise Absorption (PNA)"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"qiskit-addons/pna/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, we will learn how to leverage the latest tools in the Qiskit ecosystem to implement a fully customizable, error mitigated workflow. We will introduce the PNA technique and use it to mitigate gate errors. We will also use TREX to mitigate readout errors and post-selection to mitigate errors not captured in the learned noise model.\n"
msgstr "Dalam tutorial ini, kita akan belajar cara memanfaatkan alat-alat terbaru dalam ekosistem Qiskit untuk mengimplementasikan alur kerja mitigasi error yang sepenuhnya dapat dikustomisasi. Kita akan memperkenalkan teknik PNA dan menggunakannya untuk memitigasi kesalahan gate. Kita juga akan menggunakan TREX untuk memitigasi kesalahan readout dan post-selection untuk memitigasi kesalahan yang tidak tertangkap dalam model noise yang dipelajari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Outline**\n"
"- Give a brief overview of ``PNA``\n"
"- Create a Trotterized quantum circuit and observable. Transpile it to the backend and include post-selection measurements.\n"
"- Use ``samplomatic`` to twirl layers of 2Q gates and measurements. Find unique 2Q layers to reduce noise learning cost.\n"
"- Use ``NoiseLearnerV3`` to learn the error model affecting the 2Q gates and measurements.\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-pna`` to generate a noise-mitigating observable\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` primitive to generate the raw QPU samples reflecting every shot for every twirling randomization and measured basis\n"
"- Use ``qiskit-addon-utils`` to post-process the data into a mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Garis Besar**\n"
"- Memberikan gambaran singkat tentang ``PNA``\n"
"- Membuat Circuit Trotter kuantum dan observable. Mentranspile ke backend dan menyertakan pengukuran post-selection.\n"
"- Menggunakan ``samplomatic`` untuk men-twirl lapisan gate 2Q dan pengukuran. Menemukan lapisan 2Q unik untuk mengurangi biaya pembelajaran noise.\n"
"- Menggunakan ``NoiseLearnerV3`` untuk mempelajari model error yang memengaruhi gate 2Q dan pengukuran.\n"
"- Menggunakan ``qiskit-addon-pna`` untuk menghasilkan observable yang memitigasi noise\n"
"- Menggunakan primitif ``qiskit-ibm-runtime.Executor`` untuk menghasilkan sampel QPU mentah yang mencerminkan setiap shot untuk setiap randomisasi twirling dan basis yang diukur\n"
"- Menggunakan ``qiskit-addon-utils`` untuk memproses data menjadi nilai ekspektasi yang telah dimitigasi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"
msgstr "Apa itu propagated noise absorption (PNA)? {#what-is-propagated-noise-absorption-pna}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"***A technique for mitigating gate errors by propagating the observable through the inverse noise channel affecting 2-qubit gates, resulting in a noise-mitigating observable.***\n"
"The 2Q gates in the experiment we want to run will be affected by substantial noise.\n"
"![Noisy experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"If we learn the noise model, we can apply its inverse and cancel the noise.\n"
"![Noise-mitigated experiment](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"Instead of implementing the inverse noise channel by sampling it on the QPU as in PEC, we can implement it classically in the measured observable using Pauli propagation. This results in a more complex observable which, when measured, has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise.\n"
"![PNA overview](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"
msgstr ""
"***Teknik untuk memitigasi kesalahan gate dengan mempropagasi observable melalui saluran noise invers yang memengaruhi gate 2-qubit, menghasilkan observable yang memitigasi noise.***\n"
"Gate 2Q dalam eksperimen yang ingin kita jalankan akan dipengaruhi oleh noise yang cukup besar.\n"
"![Eksperimen berisik](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noisy_expt.png)\n"
"Jika kita mempelajari model noise, kita dapat menerapkan inversnya dan membatalkan noise tersebut.\n"
"![Eksperimen yang dimitigasi noisenya](/img/qiskit-addons/images/noise_mitigated_expt.png)\n"
"Alih-alih mengimplementasikan saluran noise invers dengan mengambil sampelnya di QPU seperti pada PEC, kita dapat mengimplementasikannya secara klasikal dalam observable yang diukur menggunakan propagasi Pauli. Ini menghasilkan observable yang lebih kompleks yang, ketika diukur, memiliki efek memitigasi noise gate yang dipelajari.\n"
"![Gambaran umum PNA](/img/qiskit-addons/images/pna_overview.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the mirrored Trotter circuit and observable {#generate-the-mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr "Buat Circuit Trotter yang dicerminkan dan observable {#generate-the-mirrored-trotter-circuit-and-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this experiment, we will study the time dynamics of a 30-site kicked Ising model on a 1D spin chain. The Hamiltonian considered is:\n"
msgstr "Untuk eksperimen ini, kita akan mempelajari dinamika waktu model kicked Ising 30-site pada rantai spin 1D. Hamiltonian yang dipertimbangkan adalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"
msgstr "$H = -J\\sum\\limits_{\\langle i,j \\rangle} Z_iZ_j + h\\sum\\limits_iX_i$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J>0$ describes the coupling of nearest-neighbor spins, $i<j$, and the global transverse field, $h$, is set to $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. The further $h$ is from a Clifford angle (i.e. $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), the more difficult it becomes to propagate the anti-noise generators through the circuit.\n"
msgstr "di mana $J>0$ mendeskripsikan kopling spin tetangga terdekat, $i<j$, dan medan transversal global, $h$, diatur ke $\\frac{\\pi}{8}$. Semakin jauh $h$ dari sudut Clifford (yaitu $\\theta=n\\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$), semakin sulit mempropagasi generator anti-noise melalui Circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the choice of observable, we will consider the average single-site magnetization, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, where $N$ is the number of sites.\n"
msgstr "Untuk pilihan observable, kita akan mempertimbangkan magnetisasi rata-rata satu site, $\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\langle z_i \\rangle$, di mana $N$ adalah jumlah site.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"
msgstr "![Diagram Circuit kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_1.png)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we will choose a chain of qubits on ``ibm_kingston`` that report low error rates and transpile the circuit to the backend.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, kita akan memilih rantai qubit di ``ibm_kingston`` yang melaporkan tingkat error rendah dan mentranspile Circuit ke backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_2.png)\n"
msgstr "![Diagram Circuit kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_2.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirl the 2-qubit gate layers and measurements and find unique layers {#twirl-the-2-qubit-gate-layers-and-measurements-and-find-unique-layers}"
msgstr "Twirl lapisan gate 2-qubit dan pengukuran serta temukan lapisan unik {#twirl-the-2-qubit-gate-layers-and-measurements-and-find-unique-layers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we ensure the pass manager annotates the boxes with ``Twirl`` and ``InjectNoise`` annotations, which allow us to learn the noise which will affect our circuit and associate that noise with its corresponding circuit layer.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita memastikan pass manager memberi anotasi pada box dengan anotasi ``Twirl`` dan ``InjectNoise``, yang memungkinkan kita mempelajari noise yang akan memengaruhi Circuit kita dan mengaitkan noise tersebut dengan lapisan Circuit yang sesuai.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``enable_gates/enable_measure: True``: Box all 2q gate layers and terminal measurements. Single qubit gates will be left-dressed within the boxes.\n"
msgstr "``enable_gates/enable_measure: True``: Jadikan box semua lapisan gate 2q dan pengukuran terminal. Gate satu qubit akan didress di kiri dalam box.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``measure_annotations: all`` Include `Twirl` and `ChangeBasis` annotations on the measurement box\n"
msgstr "``measure_annotations: all`` Sertakan anotasi `Twirl` dan `ChangeBasis` pada box pengukuran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``twirling_strategy: active``: Twirl all active qubits in each box containing entangling gates\n"
msgstr "``twirling_strategy: active``: Twirl semua qubit aktif di setiap box yang berisi gate entangling\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``inject_noise_targets: gates``: ``InjectNoise`` annotations should be added to all ``Twirl``-annotated boxes containing entangling gates\n"
msgstr "``inject_noise_targets: gates``: Anotasi ``InjectNoise`` harus ditambahkan ke semua box beranotasi ``Twirl`` yang berisi gate entangling\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``inject_noise_strategy: uniform_modification``: All of the noise layers should be scaled equivalently.\n"
msgstr "``inject_noise_strategy: uniform_modification``: Semua lapisan noise harus diskalakan secara setara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_3.png)\n"
msgstr "![Diagram Circuit kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_3.png)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate the template circuit and samplex, define how the circuit will be sampled {#generate-the-template-circuit-and-samplex-define-how-the-circuit-will-be-sampled}"
msgstr "Buat Circuit template dan samplex, tentukan cara Circuit akan diambil sampelnya {#generate-the-template-circuit-and-samplex-define-how-the-circuit-will-be-sampled}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we also add spectator and post-selection measurements, which are needed to perform post-selection on the samples output from ``Executor``.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita juga menambahkan pengukuran spectator dan post-selection, yang diperlukan untuk melakukan post-selection pada sampel yang dikeluarkan dari ``Executor``.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit diagram](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_4.png)\n"
msgstr "![Diagram Circuit kuantum](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_4.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise {#learn-the-noise}"
msgstr "Pelajari noise {#learn-the-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before we run the experiments, we learn the noise model affecting the entangling gates and measurements in the circuit. Having an accurate noise model is necessary to effectively mitigate error. Learning the noise just before executing the experiments gives the best chance of the noise model faithfully describing the actual noise affecting the gates during execution.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum kita menjalankan eksperimen, kita pelajari model noise yang memengaruhi gate entangling dan pengukuran dalam Circuit. Memiliki model noise yang akurat sangat penting untuk memitigasi error secara efektif. Mempelajari noise tepat sebelum mengeksekusi eksperimen memberikan peluang terbaik agar model noise secara akurat menggambarkan noise aktual yang memengaruhi gate selama eksekusi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before we learn the noise, we need to find the unique 2-qubit layers in our circuit, so we can minimize the number of shots needed to learn the noise for the entire circuit. We use ``find_unique_box_instructions`` from ``samplomatic`` to provide us the unique layers from the boxed circuit, including the measurement layer. These are the layers we pass to the noise learner.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum kita mempelajari noise, kita perlu menemukan lapisan 2-qubit unik dalam Circuit kita, sehingga kita dapat meminimalkan jumlah shot yang diperlukan untuk mempelajari noise untuk seluruh Circuit. Kita menggunakan ``find_unique_box_instructions`` dari ``samplomatic`` untuk mendapatkan lapisan unik dari Circuit yang di-box, termasuk lapisan pengukuran. Inilah lapisan yang kita oper ke noise learner.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once we know the layers, we can learn the noise. There are a few parameters we consider:\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita mengetahui lapisannya, kita dapat mempelajari noise. Ada beberapa parameter yang perlu dipertimbangkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_randomizations`: The number of random circuits to use per learning circuit configuration\n"
msgstr "`num_randomizations`: Jumlah Circuit acak yang digunakan per konfigurasi Circuit pembelajaran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shots_per_randomization`: Total number of shots to use per random learning circuit\n"
msgstr "`shots_per_randomization`: Total jumlah shot yang digunakan per Circuit pembelajaran acak\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`layer_pair_depths`: The circuit depths (measured in number of pairs) to use in learning experiments.\n"
msgstr "`layer_pair_depths`: Kedalaman Circuit (diukur dalam jumlah pasangan) yang digunakan dalam eksperimen pembelajaran.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`post_selection`: We will use edge-based post-selection during learning using `rx` gates to implement the post-measurement pulses\n"
msgstr "`post_selection`: Kita akan menggunakan post-selection berbasis edge selama pembelajaran menggunakan gate `rx` untuk mengimplementasikan pulsa pasca-pengukuran\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_5.png)\n"
msgstr "![Keluaran plot](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_5.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Associate circuit boxes with learned noise {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"
msgstr "Hubungkan kotak sirkuit dengan noise yang dipelajari {#associate-circuit-boxes-with-learned-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, we create a mapping between the ``InjectNoise`` reference IDs of each box to the learned noise model (`PauliLindbladMap`) affecting the entangling gates in that box.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, kita membuat pemetaan antara ID referensi ``InjectNoise`` dari setiap kotak ke model noise yang dipelajari (`PauliLindbladMap`) yang memengaruhi gate entangling dalam kotak tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Propagate the observable through the learned anti-noise to get a noise-mitigating observable {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"
msgstr "Propagasi observable melalui anti-noise yang dipelajari untuk mendapatkan observable peredam noise {#propagate-the-observable-through-the-learned-anti-noise-to-get-a-noise-mitigating-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As discussed above, this is done in two steps. First, we propagate an anti-noise generator to the end of the circuit. After that, we propagate the observable through that evolved generator. This process is repeated for each anti-noise generator in the circuit. In this implementation, each generator in a given layer is propagated to the end of the circuit in parallel. Additionally, Python multiprocessing is used to perform both the forward-propagation of the anti-noise as well as the back-propagation of the observable in parallel. This prevents a pile-up of evolved generators in memory and also maximizes compute resources.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dibahas di atas, ini dilakukan dalam dua langkah. Pertama, kita mempropagasi generator anti-noise ke akhir sirkuit. Setelah itu, kita mempropagasi observable melalui generator yang telah berevolusi tersebut. Proses ini diulang untuk setiap generator anti-noise dalam sirkuit. Dalam implementasi ini, setiap generator dalam layer tertentu dipropagasi ke akhir sirkuit secara paralel. Selain itu, multiprocessing Python digunakan untuk melakukan forward-propagation anti-noise sekaligus back-propagation observable secara paralel. Ini mencegah penumpukan generator yang telah berevolusi di memori dan juga memaksimalkan penggunaan sumber daya komputasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When running PNA, you will always need to provided a noisy circuit and observable. If your noisy circuit is a boxed circuit with `InjectNoise` annotations, you will need to provide the mapping we created in the step above. One can also pass a non-boxed circuit containing ``PauliLindbladError`` instructions from ``qiskit-aer``. In that case, ``refs_to_noise_models`` does not need to be provided. In addition to the primary inputs, users will want to consider:\n"
msgstr "Saat menjalankan PNA, kamu selalu perlu menyediakan sirkuit bernoisy dan observable. Jika sirkuit bernoisy-mu adalah sirkuit yang diberi kotak dengan anotasi `InjectNoise`, kamu perlu menyediakan pemetaan yang kita buat pada langkah di atas. Kita juga bisa memberikan sirkuit tanpa kotak yang berisi instruksi ``PauliLindbladError`` dari ``qiskit-aer``. Dalam kasus itu, ``refs_to_noise_models`` tidak perlu disediakan. Selain input utama, pengguna perlu mempertimbangkan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_err_terms`: The number of terms to keep in each anti-noise generator as it is forward-propagated. Allowing this to be larger generally increases accuracy, but this behavior is not guaranteed to be monotonic.\n"
msgstr "`max_err_terms`: Jumlah term yang disimpan dalam setiap generator anti-noise saat di-forward-propagate. Nilai yang lebih besar umumnya meningkatkan akurasi, tapi perilaku ini tidak dijamin monotonik.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_obs_terms`: The number of terms to keep in the noise-mitigating observable, $\\tilde{O}$, as it is back-propagated through the evolved anti-noise. Larger values generally increase accuracy, but it is not guaranteed to do so monotonically.\n"
msgstr "`max_obs_terms`: Jumlah term yang disimpan dalam observable peredam noise, $\\tilde{O}$, saat di-back-propagate melalui anti-noise yang telah berevolusi. Nilai yang lebih besar umumnya meningkatkan akurasi, tapi tidak dijamin monotonik.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_processes`: The number of cores to dedicate to the process. Remember, the generators are forward-propagated and applied to the observable in parallel.\n"
msgstr "`num_processes`: Jumlah core yang didedikasikan untuk proses ini. Ingat, generator di-forward-propagate dan diterapkan ke observable secara paralel.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`search_step`: The back-propagation step uses a greedy method to approximately conjugate two operators in the Pauli basis. This method can be sped up by increasing ``search_step``. See the [pauli-prop docs](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) for more info.\n"
msgstr "`search_step`: Langkah back-propagation menggunakan metode greedy untuk mengkonjugasi dua operator secara perkiraan dalam basis Pauli. Metode ini bisa dipercepat dengan menaikkan ``search_step``. Lihat [dokumentasi pauli-prop](https://qiskit.github.io/pauli-prop/) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`num_to_measure`: While this variable isn't an input to ``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, we use it to control how many terms from $\\tilde{O}$ we actually want to measure. Here we will only measure the top 30 terms, which are the original terms in our observable. The terms have now been re-scaled such that measuring them has the effect of mitigating the learned gate noise. Although we only measure 30 terms from $\\tilde{O}$, it is often still useful to allow it to grow large, as that increases the precision of the leading terms' scaling factors.\n"
msgstr "`num_to_measure`: Meski variabel ini bukan input dari ``generate_noise_mitigating_observable``, kita gunakan untuk mengontrol berapa banyak term dari $\\tilde{O}$ yang benar-benar ingin diukur. Di sini kita hanya mengukur 30 term teratas, yaitu term-term asli dalam observable kita. Term-term tersebut telah di-rescale sehingga mengukurnya memiliki efek memitigasi noise gate yang dipelajari. Meski kita hanya mengukur 30 term dari $\\tilde{O}$, sering kali tetap berguna untuk membiarkannya tumbuh besar, karena itu meningkatkan presisi faktor skala term-term terdepan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_6.png)\n"
msgstr "![Plot output](/img/qiskit-addons/pna/01-generate-noise-mitigating-observable/output_6.png)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the measurement bases to canonical form {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"
msgstr "Ubah basis pengukuran ke bentuk kanonik {#transform-the-measurement-bases-to-canonical-form}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we will find a minimal set of bases to measure such that we can fully cover every Pauli term in the measured observable (***many observables may be measured simultaneously if they commute qubit-wise***). Since we are only measuring the terms in our original observable, which is the sum of all single-`Z` Paulis, a single basis is needed -- the all-`Z` basis.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, kita akan menemukan set basis minimal untuk diukur sehingga kita bisa mencakup setiap term Pauli dalam observable yang diukur (***banyak observable bisa diukur secara bersamaan jika mereka commute secara qubit-wise***). Karena kita hanya mengukur term-term dalam observable asli kita, yang merupakan jumlah semua Pauli `Z` tunggal, hanya satu basis yang diperlukan -- basis all-`Z`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to finding a set of Pauli measurement bases, we need to map these Pauli terms to the canonical form expected by the ``Executor`` primitive. For more information on canonical qubit ordering, visit the [samplomatic docs](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"
msgstr "Selain menemukan set basis pengukuran Pauli, kita perlu memetakan term-term Pauli ini ke bentuk kanonik yang diharapkan oleh primitive ``Executor``. Untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang urutan qubit kanonik, kunjungi [dokumentasi samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/guides/samplex_io.html#qubit-ordering-convention).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify how to sample in the ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"
msgstr "Tentukan cara sampling dalam ``QuantumProgram`` {#specify-how-to-sample-in-the-quantumprogram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ``QuantumProgram`` is where we specify how to sample the experiment:\n"
msgstr "``QuantumProgram`` adalah tempat kita menentukan cara melakukan sampling eksperimen:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``template_circuit``: The circuit containing all the gates necessary to implement all desired randomizations (from twirling randomizations, parameters, etc).\n"
msgstr "``template_circuit``: Sirkuit yang berisi semua gate yang diperlukan untuk mengimplementasikan semua randomisasi yang diinginkan (dari randomisasi twirling, parameter, dll.).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samplex``: An object definining a probability distribution over all possible circuit randomizations from which to sample.\n"
msgstr "``samplex``: Objek yang mendefinisikan distribusi probabilitas atas semua kemungkinan randomisasi sirkuit untuk di-sampling.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``samplex_arguments``: Bindings necessary to fully define the samplex\n"
msgstr "``samplex_arguments``: Binding yang diperlukan untuk mendefinisikan samplex sepenuhnya\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``basis_changes``: Here is where we specify a set of bases to measure which will cover all of the Pauli terms in the measured observable.\n"
msgstr "``basis_changes``: Di sinilah kita menentukan set basis untuk diukur yang akan mencakup semua term Pauli dalam observable yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``noise_scales.ref``: We set each noise layer's scale to `0.0` to prevent any additional noise from being injected into our samples\n"
msgstr "``noise_scales.ref``: Kita setel skala setiap layer noise ke `0.0` untuk mencegah noise tambahan disuntikkan ke sampel kita.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Required if ``noise_scales`` are passed. This just maps noise layers to the associated noise model.\n"
msgstr "``pauli_lindblad_maps``: Diperlukan jika ``noise_scales`` diberikan. Ini hanya memetakan layer noise ke model noise terkait.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "``shape``: A shape tuple to extend the implicit shape defined by ``samplex_arguments``. Non-trivial axes introduced by this extension enumerate randomizations.\n"
msgstr "``shape``: Tuple shape untuk memperluas shape implisit yang didefinisikan oleh ``samplex_arguments``. Sumbu non-trivial yang diperkenalkan oleh perluasan ini mengenumerasi randomisasi.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample the circuit using the ``Executor`` primitive prototype {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"
msgstr "Sample sirkuit menggunakan prototype primitive ``Executor`` {#sample-the-circuit-using-the-executor-primitive-prototype}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have defined our ``QuantumProgram``, executing the experiment is straightforward. We simply instantiate the ``Executor`` object, provide it the backend, and run the program.\n"
msgstr "Setelah kita mendefinisikan ``QuantumProgram``, mengeksekusi eksperimen menjadi sangat mudah. Kita cukup menginstansiasi objek ``Executor``, menyediakan backend, dan menjalankan program.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the samples to calculate an error-mitigated expectation value {#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-expectation-value}"
msgstr "Post-process sampel untuk menghitung nilai ekspektasi yang telah dimitigasi errornya {#post-process-the-samples-to-calculate-an-error-mitigated-expectation-value}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To calculate an error-mitigated expectation value, we will:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menghitung nilai ekspektasi yang telah dimitigasi errornya, kita akan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the TREX scaling factors based on the learned noise affecting the measurements\n"
msgstr "Menghitung faktor skala TREX berdasarkan noise yang dipelajari yang memengaruhi pengukuran\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate a mask for keeping only post-selected samples\n"
msgstr "Membuat mask untuk menyimpan hanya sampel yang telah di-post-select\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the ``executor_expectation_values`` function from ``qiskit-addon-utils`` for combining all of the data into an error-mitigated expectation value.\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan fungsi ``executor_expectation_values`` dari ``qiskit-addon-utils`` untuk menggabungkan semua data menjadi nilai ekspektasi yang telah dimitigasi errornya.\n"

